{
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "traffic-reporter",
  "main": "src/index.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-08-15",
  "observability": {
    "enabled": true
  },
  "triggers": {
    // V1.6.1: every 10 minutes, UTC (Cloudflare Cron Triggers are always
    // UTC; UTC minutes == Asia/Taipei minutes since Taipei is a fixed
    // UTC+8 offset). PBS runs every tick (24/7). TDX (國道+省道 only —
    // see src/tdx/sources.js's PRODUCTION_TDX_SOURCE_IDS) is further
    // gated INSIDE the scheduled handler to only every 2nd tick
    // (minute 00/20/40) and only 08:00–21:59:59 Asia/Taipei — see
    // src/traffic/tdxSchedule.js. Deliberately still just ONE Cron
    // trigger, not two competing schedules — "不要建立兩套互相複雜的
    // Cron".
    "crons": ["*/10 * * * *"]
  },
  // TRAFFIC_KV was originally bound only via the Cloudflare dashboard,
  // which `wrangler deploy` silently dropped on the next deploy because
  // this file is treated as the full declarative binding set (exactly
  // the caveat this comment used to warn about). Declared explicitly now
  // with the real namespace ID from the dashboard so it survives every
  // deploy. TDX_CLIENT_ID/TDX_CLIENT_SECRET/LINE_CHANNEL_ACCESS_TOKEN/
  // LINE_CHANNEL_SECRET remain Cloudflare Secrets configured outside this
  // repo — see src/traffic/dedupe.js — and are unaffected by this change.
  //
  // V1.6.3: ADMIN_PASSWORD (HTTP Basic Auth for GET /health,
  // /debug/status, /debug/tdx, /debug/pbs, /debug/pbs-vpc-probe — see
  // src/security/adminAuth.js) is ALSO a Cloudflare Secret configured
  // outside this repo (`wrangler secret put`), never declared here —
  // this file never carries real credential values, only bindings/IDs
  // that are not secret on their own. The admin username is a fixed
  // constant ("admin") in code, not a Secret — no first-run setup page,
  // no Cookie session, no password ever stored in KV.
  "kv_namespaces": [
    {
      "binding": "TRAFFIC_KV",
      "id": "a763ccea75b0481aa4da99fa43f8341a"
    }
  ],
  // V1.8.4: CCTV_IMAGES — an R2 bucket binding for the published-collage-
  // image layer (src/cctv/publishedImage.js). Deliberately R2, not
  // TRAFFIC_KV: R2 gives strongly consistent read-after-write on
  // PUT/GET/DELETE, which the intended flow (compose -> store ->
  // immediately push to LINE -> LINE's servers GET the URL, likely from
  // a different Cloudflare location) actually needs — Workers KV is only
  // eventually consistent (Cloudflare's own docs: a write can take 60s+
  // to become visible elsewhere, and negative lookups get cached too),
  // which is unacceptable for incident-time delivery. No Secret/API
  // token is required for an R2 Worker binding.
  //
  // CONFIRMED created in Production (post-V1.8.4): bucket enabled, R2
  // lifecycle rule set to auto-delete objects after 1 day — a backstop
  // ONLY, never what determines a published-image URL's validity; that's
  // still enforced entirely in code from each object's own
  // customMetadata.expiresAt on every read (see publishedImage.js).
  "r2_buckets": [
    {
      "binding": "CCTV_IMAGES",
      "bucket_name": "traffic-reporter-cctv-images"
    }
  ],
  // V1.8.5: PUBLIC_BASE_URL — this Worker's own public HTTPS origin, NOT
  // a secret (LINE's servers already need to fetch from it with zero
  // credential — see cctv/publishedImage.js). Needed because the dynamic
  // per-accident CCTV image URL (cctv/dynamicCollage.js) is built from
  // the Cron scheduled handler, which has no incoming Request to derive
  // an origin from the way the Admin HTTP endpoints do (see
  // hsinchuCctvProbe.js's handleHsinchuCctvPublishTest). Code falls back
  // to this exact value if the var is ever absent/misconfigured, so a
  // missing var degrades safely rather than producing a broken URL.
  "vars": {
    "PUBLIC_BASE_URL": "https://traffic-reporter.mr-happytan.workers.dev",
    // TDX QUOTA PROTECTION (2026-08-23). "PBS_ONLY" stops every TDX API
    // call from the Cron path (RoadEvent freeway/highway, the OAuth token,
    // and CCTV enrichment) while 警廣 PBS keeps running unchanged.
    // TDX code is NOT removed — this is a runtime gate.
    // RESTORE: set this to "ALL" (or delete the var) and push to main.
    // Full procedure: src/traffic/sourceMode.js module comment.
    // It lives here rather than in the dashboard because Workers Builds
    // treats this file as authoritative and would overwrite a
    // dashboard-only var on the next build.
    "TRAFFIC_SOURCE_MODE": "PBS_ONLY",
    // LINE PUSH POLICY (2026-08-23). The LINE OA's monthly proactive-Push
    // allowance is limited, so proactive broadcast is temporarily narrowed
    // to accidents only: closure/control/construction/'other' anomalies and
    // 機動路肩 announcements all stop pushing. Detection of every one of
    // them is UNCHANGED — they still appear in /debug/status and the
    // Pipeline Trace; only the proactive product is withheld.
    // Set to "ALL_ELIGIBLE" to restore the previous behaviour. A typo
    // resolves to the restrictive default on purpose (the expensive
    // mistake here is pushing too much). Rule: src/traffic/broadcastPolicy.js.
    "LINE_PUSH_POLICY": "MAJOR_ACCIDENT_ONLY"
  },
  "vpc_services": [
    {
      "binding": "PBS_RELAY_WINDOWS",
      "service_id": "01a008ab-4cc4-7c22-a747-4e27cdcc83c8"
    }
  ]
}
